This solution uses the Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm to efficiently generate all prime numbers up to a specified limit. The `is_prime` function leverages the results of the sieve to quickly determine if a given number is prime. This approach significantly reduces the computational complexity compared to checking each number individually.

