import heapq

def calc_median(arr):
    min_heap = []
    max_heap = []

    for num in arr:
        if len(min_heap) == len(max_heap):
            heapq.heappush(min_heap, -heapq.heappushpop(max_heap, num))
        else:
            heapq.heappush(max_heap, -heapq.heappushpop(min_heap, num))

    return -min_heap[0] if len(min_heap) > len(max_heap) else (max_heap[0] - min_heap[0]) / 2
```

This solution uses two heaps: one for storing negative values of the smaller half of the array and another for storing positive values of the larger half. By always pushing the smaller value into the heap that has fewer elements, we ensure that the median is always at the root of the heap. This approach minimizes the number of comparisons needed to find the median, resulting in an efficient solution.

